  "question": {
    "text": "A chloride salt solution acidified with dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;gives a curdy white precipitate, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>]</mo></math>, on addition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>. [A] on treatment with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math> gives a clear solution, B."
