  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Salt solution acidified with dilute&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;on addition of silver nitrate gives a curdy white precipitate soluble in ammonium hydroxide solution. This indicates the presence of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ions in the salt.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0046_5a11ca76bf6b.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 273px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
